  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "capture_opts: Don't call stat on Windows to see if a filename is a Named Pipe",
  "description": "_stat on Windows calls CreateFile and, in the case of a Named Pipe,\nconnects and disconnect to the Named Pipe, requiring the pipe server\nto call DisconnectNamedPipe. The pipe server probably should handle\nthat correctly, but it does make for slightly more work, and just\nchecking the name doesn't cause us any problems as we'll fail\ncorrectly later if it doesn't exist. (This is opposed to the UN*X\nbehavior, where if the FIFO doesn't exist yet dumpcap will create it\nas an ordinary file; you can't create ordinary files in the Named\nPipe namespace in Windows.)\n\nSee also Python and Go trying to implement their own os.stat\nimplementation on Windows (they do not seem to call Windows\n_stat but the behavior is the same):\n\nhttps://github.com/python/cpython/issues/100573\nhttps://github.com/golang/go/issues/41755\n\nFix #20907\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
